positive_text:
Each of the $25$ cells in a $5 \times 5$ grid contains a unique integer from $1$ to $25$. You may perform the following operations:

1) Select any two adjacent cells (sharing a side) and increase one by $2$, decrease the other by $1$;
2) Select any two cells with a shared vertex and increase one by $1$, decrease the other by $1$;

a) Can the table be transformed such that all cells contain the same value using these operations?

b) Can all cells be made to contain the number $2$ using these operations?

negatives.text:
