Let triangle $ABC$ have an incircle $C_1$ that touches $AB$ at $D$ and $AC$ at $E$. The incircle $C_2$ of triangle $ADE$ touches $AB$ and $AC$ at $P$ and $Q$, respectively, and intersects $C_1$ at points $M$ and $N$. Show that
(a) the center of $C_2$ lies on the circumference of $C_1$;
(b) the quadrilateral formed by $M, N, P, Q$ is a rectangle if and only if $2r_1 = 3r_2$, where $r_1$ and $r_2$ are the radii of $C_1$ and $C_2$, respectively.

